   "id": 665474683,
   "body": "$TGT \n \nHSBC upgraded Target to Buy from Hold today and raised its target to 190 from 125. That is a 52 percent raise, sitting well above the Street average near 166. \n \nAnalyst Joe Thomas also lifted his fiscal 2027 earnings estimate to 10.61 from 8.26, up 28 percent. His case: better sales create operating leverage, pushing margins toward 6 percent. \n \nThe read behind it: second-quarter growth was traffic-driven. Shoppers visited more often instead of spending more per trip. Thomas says that shows Target is rebuilding traffic without cannibalizing its store base. \n \nThe wrinkle: Target cut prices on nearly 2,000 items Tuesday, on top of 10,000-plus over the past year. Traffic built on price cuts is real until the margin math shows up. \n \nShares around 157 today, up 63 percent on the year.",
