  {
   "id": 665387101,
   "body": "UBS has highlighted key U.S. durable-goods retailers as AI-powered shopping agents emerge, potentially reshaping how consumers discover and purchase products. \nWalmart  The retailer is positioned through a combination of partnerships with external AI platforms and investments in its own capabilities. Its scale, logistics network, pricing power and broad product selection remain important regardless of where the shopping journey begins. UBS said the key challenge may be protecting Walmart’s high-margin advertising business and broader ecosystem economics rather than simply maintaining sales growth. \nTarget   The retailer retains competitive advantages from its scale and logistics capabilities. AI agents could increasingly direct traffic toward retailers offering the strongest and most consistent value proposition, while Target will need to balance sales growth with protecting its high-margin advertising business as commerce becomes more agent-driven. \n$WMT  $TGT",
